  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Working Papers",
    "overview": "The app reads like an auditor's working paper. A pale grey-green analysis ground holds near-white sheets edged in sage hairlines; a graphite shell bar carries the module navigation and the product mark. Every figure the model returns is vouched for in pencil: a green tick when it is found on the RHP page it cites, a blue cross-reference to that page, and a numbered red query when it cannot be found. An open query blocks sign-off until a reviewer clears it, and the clearing is drawn as a tick over the query box.\n\nDensity is that of a schedule, not a dashboard: hairline-ruled tables with tabular numerals, one lead figure per panel, compact fact lists, a single tally strip. Colour is ink on paper. Green, red and blue are pencil colours with fixed meanings; everything else is graphite and sage. The world refuses the white KPI-card fintech dashboard with a blue accent and pill badges.\n\nThe world lives inside Streamlit. Every control is a standard Streamlit widget themed through `.streamlit/config.toml`; the world supplies type, palette, density and the authored SVG marks through one CSS block injected with `st.html` (never `st.markdown`, which curls the quotes inside CSS). Sheets are keyed containers (`st-key-sheet-*`, `st-key-signoff`). Streamlit strips CSS-generated text, so no copy, label or glyph may come from `::before`/`::after` content.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Graphite shell bar, grey-green ground, near-white hairline sheets.",
      "Pencil marks with fixed meanings: green tick (found), blue cross-reference (page), red numbered query (not found).",
      "Working-paper header: title and one-line purpose left, mono reference block right, 2px graphite rule below.",
      "Public Sans for all UI; JetBrains Mono only for references, codes and dates.",
      "Tabular numerals on every figure; schedules ruled, not carded."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Pencil Meaning Rule",
        "body": "Green means found, red means not found or flagged, blue means a reference, an action, or today's place on the calendar. A pencil colour is never used for decoration or for a meaning it does not carry.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Is For Queries Rule",
        "body": "Red marks only open queries and red flags. Deadlines are not queries: the calendar's last day is outlined in graphite, never red.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Clerk's Hand Rule",
        "body": "JetBrains Mono is for references, codes and dates. Prose, headings and figures are Public Sans. The one exception is a copy-ready client message shown in a Streamlit code block, which is Streamlit's copy affordance.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Heading Is The Label Rule",
        "body": "Sections are named by weight and size alone. No kicker or eyebrow sits above a heading.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper On A Desk Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces are flat. Nothing lifts on hover; a sheet's only shadow is its contact shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** vouch for every model-returned figure with a mark: tick, re-reference or numbered query.",
      "**Do** draw marks as authored inline SVG in the pencil colours.",
      "**Do** keep cross-reference blue as the single action colour, with one primary button per sheet at most.",
      "**Do** set every figure in tabular numerals and right-align numeric columns.",
      "**Do** open every page with the working-paper header and close it with the compliance footer.",
      "**Do** carry sheet styling on keyed containers (`st-key-sheet-*`, `st-key-signoff`) and inject the world CSS with `st.html`.",
      "**Do** keep every control a standard Streamlit widget."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** build white KPI cards with a blue accent and pill badges.",
      "**Don't** use red for anything but open queries and red flags; outline deadlines in graphite.",
      "**Don't** set prose, headings or figures in JetBrains Mono (copy-ready messages in code blocks excepted).",
      "**Don't** put a kicker or eyebrow label above a heading.",
      "**Don't** generate text, labels or glyphs with CSS `content`; Streamlit strips it.",
      "**Don't** inject the world CSS with `st.markdown`; it curls the quotes.",
      "**Don't** let the chart-only umber, ochre or plum leave the charts."
    ]
  }
